  "content": {
    "title": "Who is Justin Rose? What to know about age, wife and career earnings",
    "text": "Updated April 12, 2026, 4:58 p.m. ETThe day started with Rory McIlroy and Cameron Young tied for first. But as of publication, Justin Rose is in the lead to win this year's Masters, something he has attempted nearly two dozen times now with three runner-up finishes.What is Justin Rose's age?Rose was born on July 30, 1980 making him 45.Where is Justin Rose from?Rose was born in Johannesburg, South Africa and lives in London, according to his PGA biography.How many PGA Tour competitions has Justin Rose won?Rose has 13 wins under his belt, including the U.S. Open and an Olympic gold medal.Has Justin Rose won the Masters?This year marks Rose's 21st Masters. He's landed in second place three times. Two of those have been in playoff losses (2017 to Sergio Garcia and 2025 to Rory McIlroy).How much is Justin Rose worth?Rose has accumulated almost $75 million in PGA prize money throughout his career. His net worth estimate fluctuates, but it seems to hover around $40 million to $50 million. Who is Justin Rose's wife?Rose's wife is gymnast Kate Phillips. The two have been married since 2006.Does Justin Rose have any children?Rose and Phillips have a son, Leo, and a daughter, Charlotte, according to People Magazine.Justin Rose's odds of wining Masters 2026As of publication, BetMGM gives Rose the second best odds at winning the Masters at +160 behind McIlroy at +138.Miguel Legoas is a Deep South Connect Team Reporter for USA Today. Find him on Instagram @miguelegoas and email atmlegoas@gannett.com.",
